Use one of these, depending on what you mean by “terminate”:

```c
#include <stdlib.h>

int main(void) {
    return 0;          // Normal successful termination
}
```

Or explicitly:

```c
#include <stdlib.h>

int main(void) {
    exit(EXIT_SUCCESS);  // Runs registered cleanup handlers, flushes stdio
}
```

For an error exit:

```c
exit(EXIT_FAILURE);
```

If you need to stop immediately without normal cleanup:

```c
#include <unistd.h>

_exit(1);   // POSIX; does not flush stdio or run atexit handlers
```

In most cases, simply `return 0;` from `main` is the cleanest approach.
